.TH CLRU_DESTROY 3 "2026-08-02" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
clru_destroy \- destroy an LRU cache and invalidate the handle
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <clrucache.h>

clru_destroy(name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Calls __clrucache_destroy() to wait for every in-flight resolved use
of the handle to finish, evict all remaining entries (invoking the
eviction callback for each while the mutex is held), destroy the
internal map, and free all memory. Then sets name to
CLRU_CACHE_INVALID.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
name  Cache variable to destroy (will be set to CLRU_CACHE_INVALID
      after destruction)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Safe to call when name is CLRU_CACHE_INVALID (no-op). Calling this
on a stale handle (one already destroyed, sequentially by an
earlier call or concurrently by another thread) is a FATAL ERROR
(abort()/SIGABRT), not a silent double-free; see
__clrucache_destroy(3) for further detail.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clru_construct (3),
.BR __clrucache_destroy (3),
.BR clrucache_create_full (3)
